-- erwartet: C001
-- **646 -- a `section` name goes into C between quotes, and nothing escaped it.**
--
-- The `static` below declares a linker section whose name ends in a backslash. Gabbro's
-- `string` rule is *quote { char } quote* with *char = any character except quote and
-- newline* -- a backslash is an ordinary character there and means nothing. In C it means
-- the opposite, and the emitter copied the text through unchanged:
--
--     static uint64_t x __attribute__((section("a\"))) __attribute__((unused)) = 0;
--
-- The backslash escaped the closing quote, the string ran on, and `cc` said *missing
-- terminating quote character*. The checker said `2 items, 0 errors, 0 hints`.
--
-- **The same slot has three further shapes, all measured on 2026-09-02 and all past the
-- checker**: an empty name and a blank one reach the ASSEMBLER, which answers *missing
-- name*; Gabbro's own doubling form for an embedded quote lands as *junk at end of line*;
-- and a section name holding a NUL draws *null characters preserved in literal*. **Two of
-- the four are found by the compiler and two only by the assembler**, which is why this file
-- carries a compiler-visible one: `tests/beispiele.rs` compiles a poison probe with
-- `-fsyntax-only` and never assembles it.
--
-- > *That asymmetry is itself the finding one level up.* A gate that stops at
-- > `-fsyntax-only` cannot see half of what the emitter can write into a section name, and
-- > `instrumente/fuzze-erzeuger.py` compiles with `-c` for exactly this reason.
--
-- THE REPAIR, 2026-09-03 -- refused, and NOT escaped, and the asymmetry above is why
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- **Escaping was the smaller change and it is the wrong one.** Doubling the backslash makes
-- the C legal and hands the assembler a section whose name ends in one; GCC writes that
-- name into a `.section` directive **unquoted**, so the failure simply moves from `cc` to
-- `as`. *One tool further out is one tool fewer instruments look at* -- and the four shapes
-- above already show that half of this slot's damage lands there, invisible to the gate
-- this corpus actually runs.
--
-- So a `section` name is held to what a section name can BE: at least one character, each
-- of them a letter, a digit, or one of `. _ - $`. That is the set the linker's own sections
-- live in (`.text`, `.data.rel.ro`, `.init_array.65535`), and it is the set the corpus
-- uses -- **two `section` declarations in 612 files, both `.rodata`**. All four shapes fall
-- at `C001` now, including the two that only the assembler used to catch, and each refusal
-- names the character it stopped at:
--
--     section ""        it is empty
--     section " "       ` ` is not a name character
--     section "a""b"    ` ` -- adjacent string literals JOIN WITH A SPACE (`erwarte_text`),
--                       so the doubling form is not an embedded quote at all
--     section "a<NUL>b" `\0` is not a name character
--
-- > **The note beside `kommentartext` had ruled this channel closed, in writing**: a Gabbro
-- > string cannot contain a quote, so nothing can escape out of a `section` attribute. It
-- > was open by one character nobody had thought of. *A closed channel is a claim about
-- > every character, and it was checked against one.*

module gift::section_name_that_closes_the_c_string {

static mut x : u64 = 0 section "a\";

}
